+;; STUBS A STEP (labelled): set-display-type! is redefined to add the class tag but skip the
+;; keyword. A batch insert entry's display-type on its target reads back, answering 500 naming the
+;; entry, with nothing committed. Before the fix: 201, and the block tagged Code with no type.
+(deftest batch-insert-entry-read-back-test
+  (async done
+    (with-graph done 2
